WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.200
Organizational Profiles turn CSF 2.0 from a reference framework into an operating tool.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.980
A Current Profile describes the cybersecurity outcomes an organization is currently

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.080
achieving,

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.100
partially achieving, or attempting to achieve.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.720
It should be honest and evidence-based.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.500
The purpose is not to make the organization look mature.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.640
The purpose is to understand current risk and support better decisions.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.940
A Target Profile describes desired cybersecurity outcomes.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:34.360
Those desired outcomes should reflect business objectives, risk tolerance, requirements,

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:39.940
threat context, technology, supplier dependencies, and available resources.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.800
A Target Profile is not necessarily every possible outcome at maximum rigor.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.580
It is the set of outcomes the organization decides it needs for the scope being assessed.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.360
Comparing a Current Profile to a Target Profile reveals gaps and priorities.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:58.980
Some gaps may be urgent because they affect critical assets or high-risk suppliers.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:04.800
Others may be acceptable for a period of time if an owner documents the risk decision and

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.300
the improvement plan.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.440
This comparison helps teams move from general concern to specific work:

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:15.220
what outcome is missing, who owns it, what evidence exists, what improvement is

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.000
planned, and when progress will be reviewed.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.380
Profiles can be scoped in many ways.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.320
A profile might cover an entire organization, a business unit, a product,

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:30.340
a cloud environment, a critical system, a supplier relationship, or a threat

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:31.440
scenario.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:36.220
The scope should be documented clearly, along with assumptions and exclusions.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:40.280
A well-scoped Organizational Profile helps leaders, engineers,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.860
and risk teams communicate about the same set of outcomes.
